estion/math-academy-id "q-114016" :question/problem "Given that ${\\int }_{3}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-6,$ calculate\n${\\int }_{1}^{3}(8-f(x))\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{3}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can split up the given integral using the sum rule and factor out the constants. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{3}(8-f(x))\\,\\text{d}x & =8{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8\\cdot x\\,{|}_{1}^{3}-6 \\\\  & =8(3-1)-6 \\\\  & =8\\cdot 2-6 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250155 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078426 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff2f1a9d-2b0e-5a18-98d5-4f49f6f1527b" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating an Integral Given Another Integral With Reversed Limits of Integration"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27b56cc2-52b2-5ad8-b3a0-4c59592ae24c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247778} {:answer/id #uuid "3d59838f-ab0d-51f6-854d-c34124e124fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247965} {:answer/id #uuid "4cd5ec95-929c-55b9-bb40-0fa8c4f75970" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248112} {:answer/id #uuid "52fd01a3-5703-5bd9-a017-b785c7f290f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248172} {:answer/id #uuid "eb215c79-be82-57fd-a447-5866ea49ebb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249494}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "52fd01a3-5703-5bd9-a017-b785c7f290f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248172} :answer-field/id #uuid "4456ec5e-2fa3-59bb-b8db-5e645c385bd0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249793}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "78c51f41-fb2a-59de-87f9-0bb3b871e751" :question/math-academy-id "q-114019" :question/problem "Given that ${\\int }_{1}^{-1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-1,$ calculate\n${\\int }_{-1}^{1}(f(x)-6x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{1}^{-1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can split up the given integral using the sum rule and factor out the constants. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}(f(x)-6x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x-6{\\int }_{-1}^{1}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =1-6\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {x}^{2}\\,{|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =1-3({1}^{2}-(-1)^{2}) \\\\  & =1-3\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250159 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064218 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "de1e3f3a-5a64-573f-8fb1-9952fa36a839" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Indefinite Integrals Using Substitution with Inverse Sine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ae94c5a-4c0e-5d18-8e16-ca2223f1d464" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247517} {:answer/id #uuid "8779f6eb-94c4-53a0-ab68-b0042bb9935b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(6x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248636} {:answer/id #uuid "8f996840-de58-519e-9ad5-b2271f08b943" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{36}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(6x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248702} {:answer/id #uuid "a7a73405-8896-5d3b-959c-d98a3a0bf6d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(6x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248915} {:answer/id #uuid "dd1ebfa7-4b17-5af2-bcf2-93117f7bdcce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(6x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249385}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f996840-de58-519e-9ad5-b2271f08b943" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{36}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(6x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248702} :answer-field/id #uuid "d1111c22-992f-5424-8973-a294870d0e57" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250033}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "49cf1e17-5602-5d73-b695-bcf78c6bba28" :question/math-academy-id "q-114023" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{1}{6\\sqrt{1-36{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "This integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have $36{x}^{2}=(6x)^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=6x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=6\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{6}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{6\\sqrt{1-36{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{6}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(6x)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\cdot (\\frac{1}{6}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{36}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{36}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{36}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(6x)+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250162 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064182 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "90033e91-fdb2-5aa0-8cce-76762a38ffd2" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using Arcsine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "68b10feb-2180-5f4b-affc-efda6877e76e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2arccscx+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248364} {:answer/id #uuid "6aec3579-b361-56d6-a432-c946f704be8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248375} {:answer/id #uuid "da0de2de-876a-5403-b74e-22394befed75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2arcsecx+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249349} {:answer/id #uuid "ed63bc4d-a191-52f9-8099-1ca3eac1e754" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249506} {:answer/id #uuid "f89181c8-7cac-5b50-aded-bef01ac1683b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249591}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f89181c8-7cac-5b50-aded-bef01ac1683b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249591} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e8c0466-86ee-546f-9d46-8a6ca5c6d092" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249724}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "620c9fa2-b98d-514c-8603-da573e96fa60" :question/math-academy-id "q-114026" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{-2}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{-2}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =-2\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250163 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064218 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "de1e3f3a-5a64-573f-8fb1-9952fa36a839" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Indefinite Integrals Using Substitution with Inverse Sine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "73c527d9-5fef-527b-944d-6452bf1f22ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\sqrt{3}x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248439} {:answer/id #uuid "b49d7d3e-613f-5c56-842d-c0c3e5de4bcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{8}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\sqrt{3}x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249040} {:answer/id #uuid "bde79f17-dd2a-5f64-a9ae-c0fae23b5c8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(3x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249113} {:answer/id #uuid "dc9408cf-bf7c-5267-9022-0123e7766afe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\sqrt{3}x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249376} {:answer/id #uuid "ec0cf6c1-d063-5749-83ca-58271291edbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{8}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(3x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249497}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73c527d9-5fef-527b-944d-6452bf1f22ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\sqrt{3}x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248439} :answer-field/id #uuid "aaa559e6-16f4-5c76-808e-c0ea0a5329cb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249974}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "836b44bd-5d8f-5551-957e-758fcb5e8836" :question/math-academy-id "q-114027" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{8}{\\sqrt{1-3{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "This integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have $3{x}^{2}=(\\sqrt{3}x)^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\sqrt{3}x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\sqrt{3}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{8}{\\sqrt{1-3{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{8}{\\sqrt{1-(\\sqrt{3}x)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\cdot (\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{3}}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\sqrt{3}x)+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250165 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064218 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "de1e3f3a-5a64-573f-8fb1-9952fa36a839" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Inde